.TH CHTTPCLIENT_DO_STREAMING 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_do_streaming \- do an HTTP request and stream the response body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpclient_do_streaming(chttpcli cli,
                                       const chttp_request_t *req,
                                       chttpcli_write_fn write_fn,
                                       void *write_ctx,
                                       int *status_code_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function works like chttpclient_do, but instead of buffering the
response body it hands the body to write_fn in chunks as the data
arrives. It allocates no chttpcli_response struct, and you get no
access to the response headers this way.

write_fn must return the number of bytes it consumed; any value other
than len aborts the transfer with a failure. Calling
chttpclient_destroy on cli from inside write_fn is a fatal error,
because the destroy would wait for the very request that runs the
callback; see chttpclient_destroy(3).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli             The client handle. It must not be CHTTPCLI_INVALID.
req             The request to run. It must not be NULL.
write_fn        The callback that the client calls with each chunk of
                the body. It must not be NULL.
write_ctx       An opaque context pointer that the client passes to
                write_fn unchanged.
status_code_out Receives the HTTP status code when the call
                succeeds. It can be NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The same codes as chttpclient_do, with two differences. This function
never returns ccol_msg_too_large, because
chttpclient_set_max_response_body_size has no effect on a streaming
request: the caller's write_fn decides how much memory it uses. It also
returns ccol_http_transfer_aborted when write_fn returns anything other
than len, since any such value, above len or below it, aborts the
transfer.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_do (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async_streaming (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_pooled_streaming (3)
